  {
    "id": "how",
    "title": "From boxes to coordinates",
    "labels": [
      "Exit and voice",
      "Status conversion",
      "Bounded hierarchy"
    ],
    "lines": [
      "Instead of labelling whole civilizations, the book measures relationships along distinct dimensions.",
      "It asks who can leave, speak, appeal, observe decisions, and impose sanctions.",
      "Domination appears when wealth, media, office, and force convert into each other until escape disappears.",
      "Hierarchy can stay legitimate when its purpose, scope, duration, review, and exit are clear."
    ],
    "emotionalPlan": {
      "arc": "analytical build from method to the warning about closing loops, released by a constructive distinction",
      "purpose": "Show the book's method: a coordinate system of concrete questions, the danger of convertible status, and hierarchy without domination.",
      "states": [
        "methodical",
        "probing",
        "grave",
        "reassuring"
      ],
      "intensities": [
        0.4,
        0.55,
        0.75,
        0.45
      ],
      "voiceDirections": [
        "Measured and clear, as if laying out a map.",
        "Brisk list, a short beat between each verb.",
        "Slow down toward 'until escape disappears'.",
        "Warmer and calm, release the tension."
      ]
    },
